.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt FUJICLI 1
.Os fujicli
.Sh NAME
.Nm fujicli
.Nd manage Fujifilm cameras over USB
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl jv
.Op Fl d Ar bus . Ns Ar address
.Op Fl -emulate Ar vendor : Ns Ar product
.Cm device
.Cm list | info
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm simulation
.Cm list
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm simulation
.Cm get | export | import
.Ar slot
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm simulation set
.Op Ar option-flags
.Ar slot
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm backup
.Cm export | import
.Ar file
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm image render
.Op Fl -slot Ar slot | Fl -simulation-file Ar file | Fl -like Ar image
.Op Fl -draft
.Op Ar option-flags
.Ar input output
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Cm image extract
.Ar input output
.Nm
.Fl V | h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
talks to Fujifilm cameras over USB using PTP.
It reads camera information, reads and writes the film simulations stored in
the camera's custom setting slots, exports and restores the camera's settings
backup, and renders RAF files to JPEG on the camera's own image processor.
.Pp
Which models are known, and which of the features above each model supports,
is defined in FML; see
.Xr fujicli-fml 5
and
.Xr fujicli 7 .
A command that needs a feature the camera does not have fails with
.Qq camera does not support ... .
.Ss Device selection
Commands that talk to a camera use the first supported camera found on the USB
bus, or the device at
.Fl -device
if given.
A device given with
.Fl -device
must be a supported model unless
.Fl -emulate
is also given.
.Ss Standard streams
Wherever a command takes an input or output file, an argument of
.Ql -
means standard input or standard output.
.Ss Slots
A
.Ar slot
names a custom setting slot, as
.Cm C1
to
.Cm C7
or
.Cm 1
to
.Cm 7 .
Case is ignored.
The number of slots depends on the model.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are global and may appear before or after any command.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl j , Fl -json
Print results as JSON instead of text.
Applies to
.Cm device list ,
.Cm device info ,
.Cm simulation list
and
.Cm simulation get .
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Log more to standard error.
Repeat to increase verbosity: once for info, twice for debug, three times for
trace.
By default only warnings and errors are logged.
.It Fl d Ar bus . Ns Ar address , Fl -device Ar bus . Ns Ar address
Use the USB device at
.Ar bus
and
.Ar address ,
given in decimal, for example
.Ql 3.14 .
.Cm device list
prints these.
.It Fl -emulate Ar vendor : Ns Ar product
Treat the camera as the model with the given USB vendor and product IDs, in
hexadecimal, for example
.Ql 04cb:02fc .
The camera's own IDs are ignored.
Intended for trying an unlisted model with the definition of a similar one;
see
.Sx CAVEATS .
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
Given after a command, print that command's usage, including its option flags.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
Each command and subcommand has a one-letter alias, given in parentheses.
.Ss device (d)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm device list Pq Cm l
List connected supported cameras, with their name, USB ID and bus address.
Ignores
.Fl -device
and
.Fl -emulate .
.It Cm device info Pq Cm i
Print the camera's manufacturer, model, firmware version, serial number, USB
mode and battery level.
.It Cm device reverse Pq Cm r
Developer tools for adding support for a new model.
Hidden from
.Fl -help .
Each subcommand requires
.Fl -device ,
works whether or not the device is a known model, and logs the raw PTP
traffic; use
.Fl vv
to see it.
Only use these with a full backup of the camera.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm backup export Ar output , Cm backup import Ar input
Export or import a backup the way known models do.
.It Cm info
Dump the device information, USB mode and battery level.
.It Cm simulation
Dump every simulation setting of every slot.
.El
.El
.Ss simulation (s)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm simulation list Pq Cm l
List the camera's slots and the name of the simulation in each.
.It Cm simulation get Po Cm g Pc Ar slot
Print every setting of the simulation in
.Ar slot .
.It Cm simulation set Po Cm s Pc Oo Ar option-flags Oc Ar slot
Change settings of the simulation in
.Ar slot .
The given flags are merged with the slot's current settings.
The result is then checked against the camera's rules.
Some rules repair the simulation, and may change settings other than those
given; others reject it, and the command fails with the rule's message.
Nothing is written to the camera if the simulation is rejected.
See
.Sx Option flags .
.It Cm simulation export Po Cm e Pc Ar slot output
Write the simulation in
.Ar slot
to
.Ar output
as JSON.
.It Cm simulation import Po Cm i Pc Ar slot input
Read a simulation written by
.Cm simulation export
from
.Ar input
and write it to
.Ar slot ,
replacing every setting.
The file must come from the same model.
.El
.Ss backup (b)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm backup export Po Cm e Pc Ar output
Write the camera's settings backup to
.Ar output .
.It Cm backup import Po Cm i Pc Ar input
Restore a settings backup from
.Ar input .
.El
.Ss image (i)
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm image render Pq Cm r
.Op Fl -slot Ar slot | Fl -simulation-file Ar file | Fl -like Ar image
.Op Fl -draft
.Op Ar option-flags
.Ar input output
.Xc
Render the RAF file
.Ar input
on the camera and write the resulting image to
.Ar output .
.Pp
By default the image is rendered with the settings it was shot with.
Settings from at most one of the following sources are applied over it:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -slot Ar slot
The simulation in a slot of the camera.
.It Fl -simulation-file Ar file
A simulation written by
.Cm simulation export .
.It Fl -like Ar image
The simulation embedded in the MakerNotes of a JPEG taken with a Fujifilm
camera, read with
.Xr exiftool 1 .
.Ar image
may be
.Ql - .
.El
.Pp
Settings in a simulation that do not apply to rendering are ignored.
Any option flags are then applied over the result.
The merged profile is checked and repaired against the camera's rules, as for
.Cm simulation set .
.Pp
.Fl -draft
renders a lower-quality preview, which is faster.
.It Cm image extract Po Cm e Pc Ar input output
Read the simulation embedded in the MakerNotes of the JPEG
.Ar input ,
using
.Xr exiftool 1 ,
and write it to
.Ar output
as JSON.
Does not use a camera.
.El
.Ss Option flags
.Cm simulation set
and
.Cm image render
take one flag per camera setting.
The flags are generated from FML, so the set depends on the build, and
.Fl -help
groups them by category.
A flag for a setting the camera does not have is an error.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Detail
.Fl -clarity ,
.Fl -color ,
.Fl -noise-reduction ,
.Fl -sharpness ,
.Fl -smooth-skin-effect
.It Film Simulation
.Fl -color-chrome-effect ,
.Fl -color-chrome-fx-blue ,
.Fl -film-simulation ,
.Fl -grain-effect ,
.Fl -monochromatic-color-temperature ,
.Fl -monochromatic-color-tint
.It Image
.Fl -color-space ,
.Fl -file-type ,
.Fl -image-quality ,
.Fl -image-size
.It Tone
.Fl -dynamic-range ,
.Fl -dynamic-range-priority ,
.Fl -exposure-offset ,
.Fl -highlight-tone ,
.Fl -shadow-tone
.It Lens
.Fl -lens-modulation-optimizer ,
.Fl -teleconverter
.It White Balance
.Fl -white-balance ,
.Fl -white-balance-shift-blue ,
.Fl -white-balance-shift-red ,
.Fl -white-balance-temperature
.El
.Pp
.Cm simulation set
also takes
.Fl -custom-setting-name ,
the slot's name, of at most 25 characters.
.Pp
Values are parsed as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Named values
A name or one of its aliases, for example
.Ql "Classic Chrome"
or
.Ql classicchrome
for
.Fl -film-simulation .
Case is ignored, as is every character other than letters, digits,
.Ql \&.
and
.Ql - .
An unknown name is rejected, with a suggestion if one is close.
.It Numbers
A decimal number within the setting's range, and on its step, for example
.Fl -highlight-tone Ar 1.5 .
Out-of-range and off-step values are rejected with the range or step.
.Fl -exposure-offset
is rounded to the nearest step instead.
Negative values may be given as a separate argument, as in
.Fl -color Ar -2 .
.El
.Pp
The names, aliases, ranges and steps are defined in FML; see
.Xr fujicli-fml 5 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm
reads no environment variables of its own.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATH
Searched for
.Xr exiftool 1 ,
which
.Cm image extract
and
.Cm image render Fl -like
run.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Backup files
Written by
.Cm backup export
and read by
.Cm backup import .
Should only be restored to the model that wrote them.
.It Simulation files
Written by
.Cm simulation export
and
.Cm image extract ,
and read by
.Cm simulation import
and
.Cm image render Fl -simulation-file .
JSON objects with one key per setting; the keys and values depend on the model.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find the camera and show its details:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli device list
$ fujicli device info
.Ed
.Pp
Back up the camera before changing anything:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli backup export x-t5.bak
.Ed
.Pp
Show slot C1, then change its film simulation and tone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli simulation get c1
$ fujicli simulation set c1 --film-simulation "Classic Chrome" \e
    --highlight-tone -1 --shadow-tone 1.5 --grain-effect "Weak Small"
.Ed
.Pp
Copy slot 2 to slot 5:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli simulation export 2 - | fujicli simulation import 5 -
.Ed
.Pp
Render a RAW file with the simulation in slot 3, one stop brighter:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli image render --slot 3 --exposure-offset 1 DSCF0001.RAF out.jpg
.Ed
.Pp
Use a specific camera when several are connected:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fujicli -d 3.14 simulation list --json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exiftool 1 ,
.Xr fujicli-fml 5 ,
.Xr fujicli 7
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the X-T5 has been tested extensively.
The models
.Nm
knows, and the features enabled for each, are listed in
.Sx SUPPORTED CAMERAS
in
.Xr fujicli 7 .
Writing settings or backups to a camera, emulating another model, and the
.Cm device reverse
commands may leave the camera in a bad state.
Use at your own risk.
.Pp
Opening the camera requires write access to its USB device node.
On Linux this may need a
.Xr udev 7
rule for Fujifilm's vendor ID,
.Ql 04cb .
